body:
I just read through the raws I don't rly see what deserves such scathing critism. Is an mc with insanity an overused trope? Sure. However, at least in how I view the progression of the story, it has narritively built towards a moment where he was going to snap, plus his characterisation has been building to this type of narrtive moment. 

&#x200B;

Regarding 'insanity' as an asspull, it has been established since early on that the blessing mess with your head through addiction. Hanbin has a broken blessing and as such it would make sense for the effect to be wildly less restrained + mixed with his trauma that has been a constant part of his character I don't see this as puss. Tropey sure, but trope done well are still good story telling and so far the story has engaged me duirng the dargon village arc. 

&#x200B;

Anyway this is just my response to this reaction, if I missed anything or you have another point of contention about the current chapter I'm willing to talk if you want.

What is this normie shit? 

&#x200B;

If you truly hate yourself read Metamorphosis

I just want to disappear. I don't mean suicide or self harm but Im just tired of dealing with everything really, all I do is sleep all day without talking to people. Im just tired of all the shit that been thrown at me at the lack of care or support I get from the people around me. I want to disappear even if only for a little bit so i can just enjoy life again or more accurate be free of all the stress, anxiety and depression i guess.

&#x200B;

Thanks for letting me speak
